    {
      "text": "shall a man leave his father and his mother, Gen. 2:24 (Matt. 19:5; Mark 10:7; Eph. 5:31; Moses 3:24). Abraham … a father of many nations, Gen. 17:5 (Rom. 4:17). hearken unto Israel your father, Gen. 49:2. visiting the iniquity of the fathers upon the children, Ex. 20:5 (34:7; Num. 14:18; Deut. 5:9; Mosiah 13:13). Honour thy father and thy mother, Ex. 20:12 (Deut. 5:16; Matt. 15:4; 19:19; Mark 7:10; 10:19; Luke 18:20; Eph. 6:2; Mosiah 13:20). every one that curseth his father … put to death, Lev. 20:9. sum of all the congregation … after their families, by the house of their fathers, Num. 1:2. with the ensign of their father’s house, Num. 2:2. fathers shall not be put to death for the children, Deut. 24:16 (2 Kgs. 14:6; 2 Chr. 25:4). Cursed be he that setteth light by his father, Deut. 27:16. I will be his father, 2 Sam. 7:14 (1 Chr. 17:13; Heb. 1:5). Elisha … cried, My father, my father, 2 Kgs. 2:12. your fathers tempted me, Ps. 95:9 (Heb. 3:9). as a father pitieth his children, Ps. 103:13. as a father the son in whom he delighteth, Prov. 3:12. Hear, ye children, the instruction of a father, Prov. 4:1. keep thy father’s commandment, Prov. 6:20. wise son maketh a glad father, Prov. 10:1. foolish son is the calamity of his father, Prov. 19:13. fathers have eaten a sour grape, Jer. 31:29 (Ezek. 18:2). son shall not bear the iniquity of the father, Ezek. 18:20.",
