    {
      "text": "We have Abraham to our father, Matt. 3:9 (Luke 3:8). loveth father or mother more than me is not worthy, Matt. 10:37. As he spake to our fathers, Luke 1:55. I will arise and go to my father, Luke 15:18. Ye are of your father the devil, John 8:44. that he might be the father of all them that believe, Rom. 4:11. Abraham; who is the father of us all, Rom. 4:16. have ye not many fathers, 1 Cor. 4:15. fathers, provoke not your children, Eph. 6:4 (Col. 3:21). charged every one of you, as a father doth his children, 1 Thes. 2:11. Rebuke not an elder, but entreat him as a father, 1 Tim. 5:1. spake in time past unto the fathers, Heb. 1:1. Without father, without mother, without descent, Heb. 7:3. what son is he whom the father chasteneth not, Heb. 12:7. had fathers of our flesh which corrected us, Heb. 12:9.",
